<Layout title="About"><div class="page-head"><p class="eyebrow">ABOUT THE COLLECTION</p><h1>Follow the work.<br/><em>Find the artist.</em></h1></div><article class="prose about"><p>AI Film Journal is an ongoing editorial collection of filmmakers and their work. We follow complete stories, recurring worlds and artists developing a body of work with AI.</p><h2>What makes the collection</h2><p>We look for narrative films, sustained creative direction, and ambition beyond an isolated model test. Shorts, features, and series all have a place here. Inclusion is a reason to explore a work, not a star rating or a claim that every film has been independently reviewed.</p><h2>Clear about what is known</h2><p>Each film links to its sources and carries a date checked. We distinguish public releases, festival screenings, and forthcoming films. Budgets and production methods reported by a filmmaker or studio are attributed to them. Release dates and availability can change.</p><h2>Watch at the source</h2><p>Watch links take you to filmmakers, festivals, or official distributors. Films are not hosted here. Stills, posters, and video thumbnails are credited to their respective creators or publishers and used to identify the works discussed.</p><h2>A living journal</h2><p>New discoveries and meaningful changes appear as dated journal entries. Existing artist and film pages are updated as the work develops.</p></article></Layout>
